.TH geectl-remote-delete-package 1  "geectl-remote-delete-package 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-delete\-package \- Delete a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the deletion. Without `\-\-force` a package with open submit requests is refused
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote delete\-package\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-message\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the deletion. Without `\-\-force` a package with open submit requests is refused
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Delete even when open submit requests involve the package
.TP
\fB\-\-message\fR \fI<MESSAGE>\fR
A message recorded on the delete, sent as the server\*(Aqs `comment` query parameter
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package lives in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to delete
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
